// # oodar/docs — Per-Package Documentation
//
// Logline: Per-package docs for the oodar host. Six .oot
//          files cover caps, build, tests, the
//          per-symbol coverage map, and the HW boundary.
//
// Setup: RFC-0005. Website Source: openOODA/oodar/docs/.
//        The 6 .oot files are the package manual. Each file
//        is at most 256 lines per RFC-0003.
//
// Beats:
//   1. security_model.oot      — the 26-token cap system, the 4 hard rules, the 6-step cap flow.
//   2. capabilities_table.oot  — 20 implemented + 6 future-state cap tokens.
//   3. build_and_install.oot   — canonical , per-file compile, polyrepo, liboodar.a.
//   4. testing.oot             — the 8D Red Team matrix and the 11 tier-5 tests_challenger_*.c files + 3 lint tests.
//   5. testing_coverage.oot    — per-symbol 8D coverage map (Beat 5 table, split from testing.oot for the 256-line cap).
//   6. hw_boundary.oot         — hardware-boundary inventory: 112 umbrella files by OS contact.
//
import "security_model.oot";
import "capabilities_table.oot";
import "build_and_install.oot";
import "testing.oot";
import "testing_coverage.oot";
import "hw_boundary.oot";
